  "all_ingredients_flat": "1 cup of tiger nut flour, 1 cup of brown rice flour, 1/2 cup - 3/4 cup kala chana chickpea flour, 1 Tbsp sesame seeds, 1 tsp turmeric powder, 1.5 tsp garlic powder, 1 Tbsp kasuri methi (crushed), 1/2 crushed ajwain (carom seeds), A pinch of hing (asafetida), 1 tsp Chaat Masala, Salt to taste, Pinch of baking soda, lukewarm water",
  "instructions": "DOUGH: Mix all ingredients. Bind with some lukewarm water. Let the dough rest for about 5-10 minutes.\nBAKE: Spread the dough in a baking tray. Flatten it out with the palm of your hand or with a back of a small steel bowl. Cut into desired shapes (see pic). Bake at 400F for about 10-12 mins, flipping once in between. Cooking time varies from oven to oven — it may cook faster in your oven.",
